  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_16. Let triangle PQR be a right triangle with sides PQ = 9, QR = 12. Let triangle XYZ be a right triangle with sides XY = 6. Triangle PQR is similar to triangle XYZ by AA similarity (congruent angle pairs: Q \u2245 Y, R \u2245 Z). Find the length of YZ in XYZ.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A surveyor is working with two similar right triangles to measure distances across a piece of land. In the first triangle PQR, the two legs measure PQ = 9 feet and QR = 12 feet, with the right angle at Q. The surveyor has identified a second similar right triangle XYZ (with angles matching: Q \u2245 Y and R \u2245 Z) where one leg measures XY = 6 feet and the right angle is at Y.\n\nUsing the proportional relationships between these similar triangles, what is the length of side YZ in triangle XYZ?"
